scripts/temp-password-check.mjs against REAL native GoTrue
=========================================================

The browser suite the previous backend report listed as "the F-01 bypass step
was added to temp-password-check.mjs and is not yet executed". It is executed
here, driven through the real application (`next start`) against the
native-auth stack: real GoTrue on /auth/v1, real PostgREST on /rest/v1.

HONEST NOTE ON STABILITY. The suite passes, and the run below is a passing run.
It is NOT yet stable enough for CI. Counting only the runs made with both
selector fixes in place - the state that is committed - five of seven came back
clean and two failed at the pre-existing step "a wrong temporary password is
refused", because the error alert had not rendered within its 45s window.
(Earlier runs, before those fixes, failed more often; they are not counted here
because that code is not what shipped.) GoTrue answers that request correctly and quickly (its log shows
the expected 400 on /token), so the race is in the client render, not in Auth
and not in the remediation. Two ambiguous `button[type="submit"]` selectors
were made deterministic as part of this work, which removed most of it; the
remainder belongs to whoever owns the browser suites, and until it is gone this
suite stays out of CI rather than being added as an intermittent job.

✔ staff signed in
✔ a temporary password was generated and shown once (••••-••••)
✔ signing in with it goes straight to "Choose your password" (/change-password)
✔ on a temporary password, / sends them back to choose a password
✔ on a temporary password, /savings sends them back to choose a password
✔ on a temporary password, /profile sends them back to choose a password
✔ on a temporary password, /loans sends them back to choose a password
✔ on a temporary password, /staff sends them back to choose a password
✔ on a temporary password, /admin sends them back to choose a password
✔ through the REST API the temporary password reads no records (0 rows)
✔ the retired log_password_changed() RPC is refused (42501)
✔ after the bypass attempt the temporary password still reads nothing (0 members, 0 transactions, must_change_password=true)
✔ a member's own token cannot call either half of a verified password change (42501/42501)
✔ and the open session is still confined to "Choose your password" (/change-password)
✔ a wrong temporary password is refused
✔ after choosing a password the member lands on their dashboard (/)
✔ and every member page opens
✔ the temporary password no longer works
✔ their own password does
✔ reset again at the end: the member is left on a temporary password nobody has seen

